Sval: session restore keeps a tab's undiscardable attribute

Keep Loaded marks a tab undiscardable, which TabUnloader already honours
(isNonDiscardable). Session restore keeps only the attributes
TabAttributes lists, so without it a tab would lose the mark on every
restart. An extension's autoDiscardable: false survives a restart too.

diff --git a/browser/components/sessionstore/TabAttributes.sys.mjs b/browser/components/sessionstore/TabAttributes.sys.mjs
index ea53156d12..0b30f358f9 100644
--- a/browser/components/sessionstore/TabAttributes.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/sessionstore/TabAttributes.sys.mjs
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
  * You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. */
 
 // Tab attributes which are persisted & restored by SessionStore.
-const PERSISTED_ATTRIBUTES = ["customizemode"];
+const PERSISTED_ATTRIBUTES = ["customizemode", "undiscardable"];
 
 // A set of tab attributes to persist. We will read a given list of tab
 // attributes when collecting tab data and will re-set those attributes when
